1. SCOPE
1.1 Purpose. This Technical Specification (TS) defines the functional, performance, interface, environmental, and
logistics requirements for a Multi-Band Electro-Optical / Infrared (EO/IR) Sensor Payload Suite (hereafter “the
Payload”) suitable for installation on Government-furnished High-Altitude Long-Endurance Unmanned Aerial Systems
(HALE-UAS). The Payload shall provide day/night, all-weather detection, recognition, and identification capability
against personnel, vehicles, and low-observable maritime surface targets at stand-off ranges consistent with HALE
operating altitudes of 45,000 to 65,000 feet Mean Sea Level (MSL).
1.2 Applicability. This TS applies to all contractor deliverables under Solicitation HSCBP-24-C-00087 and any
subsequent production, sustainment, or modification contracts that reference this document. Compliance with every
shall-statement is mandatory unless a formal deviation or waiver has been approved in writing by the Contracting
Officer’s Technical Representative (COTR).
1.3 System Overview. The Payload consists of a stabilized multi-sensor turret, onboard processing unit, data-link
interface electronics, power conditioning module, and associated cabling and mounting hardware. The turret houses a
high-definition visible-band camera, a mid-wave infrared (MWIR) imager, a short-wave infrared (SWIR) imager, a laser
rangefinder / designator, and an inertial measurement unit (IMU) for geo-location. The system is required to operate
continuously for mission durations up to 30 hours without ground intervention other than periodic command uplinks.
2. APPLICABLE DOCUMENTS
2.1 Government Documents. The following documents form a part of this specification to the extent specified herein.
