7.3 Acceptance Test Procedure. Every production unit shall undergo an Acceptance Test Procedure (ATP) that
verifies critical performance parameters, BIT functionality, and interface compliance. The ATP shall be approved by the
Government prior to first use. A Certificate of Conformance (CoC) shall accompany each delivered unit.
8. QUALITY ASSURANCE PROVISIONS
8.1 Quality Management System. The contractor shall maintain a Quality Management System certified to SAE
AS9100D (or equivalent) and shall flow down applicable quality requirements to all subcontractors and suppliers of
critical items listed in Table 4-1.
8.2 Configuration Management. All design artifacts, software baselines, and manufacturing process documentation
shall be placed under formal configuration control. Changes affecting form, fit, function, or interfaces shall be submitted
as Engineering Change Proposals (ECPs) and require Government approval before implementation on deliverable
hardware.
8.3 Inspection and Audit Rights. The Government reserves the right to conduct quality audits, process reviews, and
source inspections at the contractor’s and major subcontractors’ facilities with five working days’ notice. The contractor
shall provide reasonable facilities and access to records.
9. PACKAGING, HANDLING, STORAGE, AND TRANSPORTABILITY
The Payload and all LRUs shall be packaged in reusable transit cases that protect against the storage environments
listed in Table 6-1. Cases shall include desiccant, humidity indicator cards, and shock
-------------
