LING, STORAGE, AND TRANSPORTABILITY
The Payload and all LRUs shall be packaged in reusable transit cases that protect against the storage environments
listed in Table 6-1. Cases shall include desiccant, humidity indicator cards, and shock watches. The complete system
in its transit case shall not exceed 120 kg and shall be capable of being handled by a two-person lift team. Marking
shall comply with MIL-STD-129R. Each case shall be labeled with the part number, serial number, contract number,
and a unique barcode readable by standard CBP logistics systems.
10. NOTES
10.1 Intended Use. The Payload is intended for persistent wide-area surveillance in support of border security,
maritime domain awareness, and related homeland-security missions. It is not intended for use on manned aircraft
without additional certification.
