10.2 Definitions. For the purposes of this specification the following definitions apply: (a) Critical Failure – any failure
that prevents the Payload from performing its primary detection or geo-location function; (b) Organizational Level –
maintenance performed by Government or contractor personnel at the operating location using only the supplied tool
kit and spares; (c) CEP50 – Circular Error Probable, the radius of a circle centered on the true location that contains 50
% of the measured points; (d) NEdT – Noise Equivalent differential Temperature, a measure of thermal sensitivity of an
infrared sensor.
10.3 Revision History. Rev A – Initial release (12 Mar 2024). Rev B – Updated power and mass allocations; added
SWIR range requirement (28 May 2024). Rev C – Incorporated industry comments; expanded BOM table; added
software/cybersecurity section; clarified verification methods (15 Jul 2024).
10.4 Point of Contact. Technical questions regarding this specification should be directed to the Contracting Officer’s
Technical Representative (COTR) identified in the solicitation. Formal requests for clarification or deviation must be
submitted through the Contracting Officer.
