3.2 Interface Requirements.
3.2.1 Electrical Power. The Payload shall accept aircraft power conforming to MIL-STD-704F, Category A, 28 VDC
nominal. Inrush current shall not exceed 80 A for more than 50 ms. The power conditioning module shall provide
isolated outputs of +28 V, +15 V, - 15 V, and +5 V with ripple not exceeding 50 mV p-p.
3.2.2 Data Interfaces. Primary command and control shall be via dual redundant 1000BASE-T Ethernet ports
conforming to IEEE 802.3. Video streams shall be provided as ARINC 818-3 (Fibre Channel) at 3.1875 Gbps and as
compressed H.265 over Ethernet. A discrete discrete RS-422 serial channel shall be provided for legacy autopilot
health monitoring at 115 200 baud, 8N1.
3.2.3 Mechanical Interface. The turret shall mount to a Government-furnished hard-point using a 12-bolt pattern
defined in ICD-HALE-TURRET-07 Rev B. Maximum protrusion below the aircraft skin shall not exceed 420 mm.
Vibration isolators shall attenuate aircraft structure-borne vibration by a minimum of 20 dB above 50 Hz.
3.3 Reliability, Maintainability, and Availability.
The Payload Mean Time Between Critical Failures (MTBCF) shall be no less than 2
