5. SOFTWARE AND FIRMWARE REQUIREMENTS
5.1 General. All software and firmware resident in the Payload shall be developed in accordance with a tailored
application of DO-178C DAL C for flight safety-related functions and DAL D for mission functions. The contractor shall
maintain a Software Configuration Index and deliver source code, build scripts, and executable images under the
Contract Data Requirements List (CDRL).
5.2 Operating System and Middleware. The Video Processing Unit shall run a real-time operating system (RTOS)
that provides deterministic scheduling with worst-case interrupt latency not exceeding 15 µs. Approved RTOS
candidates include VxWorks 7, Integrity-178, or Linux with PREEMPT_RT patch, subject to Government approval of
the safety case.
5.3 Cybersecurity. The Payload shall implement the cybersecurity controls identified in CBP-ARCH-2022-03 Appendix
D. At a minimum this includes: (a) mutual authentication of all Ethernet command links using certificates issued by the
CBP Public Key Infrastructure; (b) encryption of all video and telemetry streams using AES-256; (c) secure boot with
measured boot attestation; and (d) a hardware root of trust that prevents unauthorized firmware loading. The contractor
shall provide a System Security Plan (SSP) and perform a Security Assessment in accordance with NIST SP 800-53
Rev 5, moderate baseline.
5.4 Software Version Identification. Every executable load shall embed a unique version identifier that is readable via
the BIT interface and via a dedicated maintenance connector. The format shall be Major.Minor.Patch-Build (example:
3.2.1-0047). Field updates shall be possible via the Ethernet maintenance port without removing the Payload from the
aircraft.
